# The prover keeps 2^k-1 in an int and builds a 2^k-entry residue table, so a
# modulus wider than 30 bits has neither a representable value to reduce against
# nor a table that fits. Refuse it at the option rather than overflow later.
#
# The error aborts the script, so this width gets a file of its own; -min-mod-bits
# is bounded by the same constant on the same shape of check.
logger -expect error "-max-mod-bits must be in 1\.\.30" 1
opt_modred -div-cells -max-mod-bits 31
